{"_id":"6a2ff9da2204ffbc59e5a7f9","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"Dj8Ar4-NQ5mQQhNHmQJVy","description":"# Categorical Plots\n\nSeaborn's categorical plots visualize the relationship between a numeric variable and one or more categorical variables. `sns.boxplot()`, `sns.violinplot()`, `sns.barplot()`, `sns.stripplot()`, and `sns.countplot()` cover the main patterns. They are used to compare distributions or averages across groups.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Visualizing categorical data","url":"https://seaborn.pydata.org/tutorial/categorical.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb79"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T13:10:50.737Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/Dj8Ar4-NQ5mQQhNHmQJVy.md"}